cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Multi-objective optimisation of the X2 expansion tube free-piston driver
message: If you use this software, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Heffernan
    given-names: Liam
    affiliation: The University of Queensland
license: MIT
abstract: >-
  Multi-objective CMA-ES for the X2 expansion tube free-piston driver,
  maximising driver hold time while minimising piston impact speed subject
  to a primary shock speed constraint. Candidate designs are evaluated with
  the L1d4 quasi-one-dimensional flow solver. Infeasible offspring are
  handled by the Arnold and Hansen (2012) covariance adaptation, and the
  shock-speed constraint by an Augmented Lagrangian.
keywords:
  - expansion tube
  - free-piston driver
  - multi-objective optimisation
  - CMA-ES
  - constraint handling
  - augmented Lagrangian
